---
title: "setLegionAddress (LegionAddressRegistry)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_caller: caller sets address in registry
    q_check_caller --> q_check_id: caller is authorized (owner/admin)
    q_check_caller --> q_revert_auth: unauthorized
    q_check_id --> q_check_addr: identifier is valid (non-empty)
    q_check_id --> q_revert_id: invalid identifier
    q_check_addr --> q_set: address != address(0)
    q_check_addr --> q_revert_addr: zero address
    q_set --> [*]: registry[identifier] = newAddress, emit AddressSet(identifier, newAddress)
    q_revert_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_revert_id --> [*]: revert InvalidIdentifier
    q_revert_addr --> [*]: revert ZeroAddress

    note right of q_set
        INV-001: Registry is central source of truth for Legion infrastructure addresses
        INV-002: Address changes propagate to sale contracts via syncLegionAddresses
    end note
